# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not,
# so never put a real key here.
#
# FMCSA_WEB_KEY is the only variable this app requires. There are no others:
# nothing else is read from the environment, and the app builds and boots
# without this one set (it renders a setup panel instead of crashing).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Getting a free webKey — steps verified against the live portal 2026-08-16
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   1. Open https://mobile.fmcsa.dot.gov/QCDevsite/docs/getStarted
#   2. Sign in via the "Sign In" link, which redirects to Login.gov. A free
#      Login.gov account is all that is needed; there is no separate FMCSA
#      registration and no approval wait.
#      Background on the Login.gov step:
#        https://mobile.fmcsa.dot.gov/QCDevsite/logingovInfo
#   3. Once signed in, choose "My WebKeys" -> "Get a new WebKey".
#   4. Fill in the form. It asks for an application name, whether the use is
#      commercial / non-commercial / academic, a rough user count, a short
#      description, and a "client secret" — the last is just a unique word you
#      pick to seed the key generator, and it must differ per WebKey.
#   5. Click create. The WebKey is shown on the next screen. Paste it below.
#
# Check it works before deploying anything, substituting your own key:
#   curl "https://mobile.fmcsa.dot.gov/qc/services/carriers/4581509?webKey=YOURKEY"
# A good key returns JSON with a "carrier" object inside "content". A bad one
# returns HTTP 404 with {"content":"Webkey not found"} — see README.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why this is not NEXT_PUBLIC_
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QCMobile takes the credential as a URL query parameter, so any code holding
# it also holds something that must never reach a browser. It is read only in
# src/lib/fmcsa/config.ts, which imports "server-only" so that the build fails
# rather than succeeds if a client component ever pulls it in. The absent
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is the other half: Next inlines only NEXT_PUBLIC_* into
# client bundles. Renaming this variable to NEXT_PUBLIC_FMCSA_WEB_KEY would
# publish your key to every visitor.
FMCSA_WEB_KEY=
